# Privacy Guard MCP

Before sending Channel Message text that may contain secrets to any model, call the `privacy-guard` MCP tools. Mapping values never leave this machine.

1. `sanitize` first. Work only on `safe_text` plus `mapping_id`.
2. `redaction_report(mapping_id)` when showing what was redacted — counts per Category, never real values.
3. `restore` before returning real values to the user.
4. Never log Mapping values, API keys, or `.env` secrets.

```text
sanitize("…192.168.1.105… sk_live_abc123…")
→ safe_text with [IP_ADDRESS_…] [API_KEY_…]
→ redaction_report → {"IP_ADDRESS": 1, "API_KEY": 1}
→ restore before the human sees the reply
```
